al downwards slightly or attempt another incremental increase, always aiming to maximize my utility while appearing cooperative.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "15f80347-b870-417e-9531-4f73c263a439"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>11</VALUE> is not feasible due to the range limit, so adjusting to <VALUE>10</VALUE> could be a reasonable step to explore higher values within the allowed range while maximizing our potential agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly noting whether Analyst A and Builder B push back against moving to the extreme end of the range or embrace it, which could provide insights into their utility functions and guide my subsequent adjustments.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "15f80347-b870-417e-9531-4f73c263a439"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly noting whether Analyst A and Critic C are willing to move away from the upper limit of the range. Depending on their responses, I might adjust my proposal further downwards or try to stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to all, aiming to infer more about their utility functions and guide my adjustments to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "15f80347-b870-417e-9531-4f73c263a439"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nThis slight increase from the current proposal seems reasonable as we explore the upper bounds of our shared range, aiming for a mutually beneficial agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly noting whether Builder B and Critic C are willing to move towards or away from this value, which could provide further insights into their utility functions and guide my subsequent adjustments.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "15f80347-b870-417e-9531-4f73c263a439"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this value to avoid unn