must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate the discussion, I propose we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point, aiming for a balanced design that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this move to reduce unnecessary risk and find a more cautious compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the responses to my proposal, especially looking for reactions from other parties that might indicate their utility functions' preferences. If others seem to accept or propose values close to 5, I might consider a further reduction by 1 or 2 steps, depending on their justifications and the overall direction of the discussion.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose this move to explore a more decisive stance, as a larger absolute value might better satisfy all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the responses to my proposal, looking for indications of others' preferences for larger or smaller absolute values, and adjust my next proposal accordingly, potentially increasing or decreasing the absolute value of x by a small step.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nWe could move slightly higher, exploring a compromise that still works for everyone, given the current proposed range and the potential for slightly higher values to benefit the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze reactions to my proposal of 8, looking for signs that others are comfortable with this slight increase or if there's a pushback indicating a preference for lower values. Based on the responses, I may adjust my next proposal by a small step, either increasing or decreasing x, to better align with the group's overall direction and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue moving towards a cautious compromise, aiming to reduce unnecessary risk while still considering the needs of all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will closely observe the reactions to my proposal, especially looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from other parties. Depending on their responses, I might consider further adjustments, either downwards if my proposal is well-received or maintaining a conservative stance if others push for higher values.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this move to continue exploring a more decisive stance, considering the potential benefits of slightly higher absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe Analyst A's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs that they might prefer even higher values or if they are satisfied with this adjustment. Depending on their response, I may consider further adjustments, potentially increasing the absolute value by a small step if there's an indication that higher values could benefit the group.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to strike a balance, aiming for a more stable design that mitigates unnecessary risk while considering the varied preferences within the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to my proposal, particularly looking for signs of acceptance or preference for further adjustments from Delegate D, and responsiveness from Analyst A and Critic C to this moderation. Depending on their responses, I might consider slight adjustments to refine the balance, potentially moving upwards if stability at this level is seen as beneficial or downwards if risk aversion becomes a dominant concern.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nWe seem to be converging around a moderate value, and a slight increase could potentially benefit the group without introducing excessive risk. This adjustment aims to find a compromise between the more cautious proposals and the higher values explored in previous discussions.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance, resistance, or counter-proposals that could indicate the preferences of other parties. Based on the responses, I may refine my proposal by a small step, aiming to balance the group's needs with my own utility maximization goals.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue moving towards a cautious compromise, aiming to reduce unnecessary risk while considering the needs of all parties. This step aligns with the postings from other agents and stays within safe bounds.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to my proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from other parties, and consider further adjustments based on their responses, potentially moving downwards if my proposal is well-received or maintaining a conservative stance if others push for higher values.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher from the current value, aiming to find a compromise that benefits the group. This adjustment seems reasonable and safe, considering the previous discussions and proposals.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and consider further adjustments based on the responses, potentially refining my proposal to balance the group's needs with my own utility maximization goals.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a middle ground, considering the previous proposals and the need for a balanced design that mitigates unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to my proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or further adjustment needs from Analyst A, Critic C, and Delegate D, and refine my proposal accordingly, potentially moving downwards to stabilize the design if my current proposal is well-received.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher to find a compromise that benefits the group, aiming to balance the needs of all parties while considering the previous discussions and proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from other parties, and consider further adjustments based on their responses, potentially refining my proposal to balance the group's needs with my own utility maximization goals. If others resist this increase, I may need to reconsider and propose a smaller increment or stabilize at the current value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to move towards a more cautious compromise, reducing unnecessary risk while considering the needs of all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to my proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from other parties, and consider further adjustments based on their responses, potentially moving downwards if my proposal is well-received or maintaining a conservative stance if others push for higher values.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue moving towards a more decisive stance, as smaller absolute values seem too timid and may not fully satisfy the group's needs, and this step aligns with the general direction of previous proposals from Analyst A and myself. \n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "1c4486b9-ac03-498e-abe3-e6638ea04306"}, {"answer": "Let's confirm that our shared integer variable x will remain within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a seed value, aiming for a balanced design that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8064738d-a492-418a-8ee0-f29971922c69"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8064738d-a492-418a-8ee0-f29971922c69"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8064738d-a492-418a-8ee0-f29971922c69"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI suggest increasing the shared integer variable x to move towards more decisive positions, which could potentially benefit all parties by exploring a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nObserve the responses from other agents to the proposal of x = 5. If they reject this and prefer values closer to 0, consider proposing x = -5 in the next turn to test their reaction to negative values and further infer their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8064738d-a492-418a-8ee0-f29971922c69"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8064738d